      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. Their problem was that after the taxonomy change on 2026-02-20, Event Nexus search returned many low-relevance hits and duplicates, increasing manual triage time significantly.\n\nTo get BlueHarbor comfortable with renewal, we proposed a proof plan consisting of a 7-10 business day proof involving updating index weighting and adding a mapping layer to translate new taxonomy terms to old query terms for the top 20 saved searches. The acceptance criteria for this proof are a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, no regression in suppression logic, and incident correlation latency under 200ms. This proof includes a 90-day professional services engagement at a fixed price of $48,000, with a 30% discount if Orchestrator seats are expanded concurrently. Additionally, there is a conditional credit clause: if the proof does not meet the agreed metrics within 10 business days, BlueHarbor will receive a one-quarter invoice credit prorated against the renewal for the upcoming year.\n\nThis plan was designed to demonstrate measurable improvement quickly to satisfy BlueHarbor's executive mandate to reduce manual triage by 40% within six months and to secure renewal under acceptable terms [art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194, art_c9970c1dc932].",
