      "answer": "The approved live patch window for Verdant Bay is on 2026-03-24 from 02:00 to 04:00 local time, as granted and customer approved. The live patch steps include draining the worker pool incrementally, deploying the ruleset branch atomically, triggering cache invalidation, and running validation jobs with synthetic and in-flight approvals.\n\nIf any validation check fails during the live patch, the rollback procedure is to use the command `orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>`, which rehydrates the prior rules and replays the invalidation hook. After rollback, Verdant Bay is notified, an incident is opened for manual remediation, and any partial replays are reverted.\n\nThis rollback is automatic if validation fails, ensuring a safe fallback to the pre-patch ruleset. Additionally, a snapshot of audit logs is taken before patching for evidence, and a replay job is scheduled the next day to re-run affected playbooks in dry-run mode with idempotency checks to avoid duplicate approvals.\n\nContacts for support during the patch include SE on-call Jin Park, Support Lead Olivia Grant, and CSM Carlos Mendes. The patch and rollback process is documented in the emergency playbook and includes telemetry verification and audit log exports for compliance.\n\nAll these details are from the Orchestrator Emergency Playbook for Verdant Bay and the Renewal Negotiation call notes [art_fff67d92fe41, art_f893faeda15a].",
