      ],
      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. They are currently running a tactical proof of concept (PoC) with NoiseGuard, a lower-cost competitor positioned for tactical noise reduction, due to a degradation in search relevance and entity graph linking after a taxonomy change. The risk of defection is high if Northstar misses acceptance milestones, as procurement may extend NoiseGuard usage and reduce Northstar's scope [art_e2727db588de, art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_7373b64fdfdd].\n\nThe exact milestone that must be met to mitigate this risk is the acceptance of the remediation plan for the taxonomy change incident. This includes:\n\n1. Verification of schema registry compatibility and collection of taxonomy snapshot by 2026-03-22.\n2. Building a shadow index scoped to warehouse/facility assets during 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-09.\n3. Backfilling enrichment and recomputing index weights from 2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30.\n4. Validation window from 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14 with acceptance criteria:\n   - precision@10 >= 0.8 for facility lookups,\n   - entity-link hit rate >= 90%,\n   - grouping false positives <= 5%.\n\nFailure to meet these acceptance criteria by the agreed dates triggers a one-time credit of 10% of ACV ($42,000) and risks customer defection to NoiseGuard [art_7373b64fdfdd, art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_79cf94421871].\n\nTherefore, Pioneer Freight Solutions is the customer most at risk of defecting to NoiseGuard if the milestone of acceptance of the remediation plan (with the above timeline and criteria) is missed.",
