      "answer": "There is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts, not just MapleBridge as a one-off. The customers sharing this failure pattern are:\n\n- MapleBridge Insurance\n- MapleFork Franchise Systems\n- MapleWest Bank\n- MapleBay Marketplace\n- MapleRegional Transit Authority\n- MaplePath Career Institute\n- City of Verdant Bay\n\nThe shared failure pattern in plain English is that after migrating from legacy workflow tooling to the Orchestrator product, approval workflows for Canada-specific policies are failing due to incorrect evaluation order of approval rules. Specifically, global default rules are overriding or bypassing region-specific (country or province) approval rules because of precedence bugs in the rules evaluation engine. This causes approval requests that should be routed to Canada-specific approvers to be either skipped, auto-denied, stuck in pending state, or routed incorrectly to global approvers. The root causes include:\n\n- Rule evaluation order prioritizing global-default rules over province or city overrides.\n- Schema key mismatches (e.g., 'country_code' vs 'country') causing rules not to match as expected.\n- Delayed synchronization of schema registry versions across evaluation clusters.\n- Missing or ambiguous rule metadata leading to fallback to global defaults.\n- Migration scripts not preserving explicit precedence or region override flags.\n\nThis results in automated approvals being bypassed or blocked, manual escalations increasing, and audit trails missing or incomplete. Customers have reported significant operational impact, including approval backlogs, misapproved claims, and compliance risks. Mitigations involve deploying override rules to force manual approvals, patching the rules evaluation engine to respect region override precedence, adding audit logging and evidence exports, and improving migration tooling to preserve rule metadata and schema compatibility.\n\nThis pattern is documented in multiple support tickets and playbooks for these customers, with coordinated hotfixes, override rules, audit evidence exports, and rollback plans being implemented to resolve the issue and prevent recurrence [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_3db205cb21ca, art_e697b3abe158].",
